+
+## Archive & size policy
+
+Keeping clones fast and reviewable needs explicit budgets for tracked
+artifacts (audit inventory findings `INV-P2-001`, `INV-P2-002`):
+
+- **Generated source snapshots are not committed.** Full-repository `repomix`
+  exports are reproducible on demand and are excluded by `.repomixignore`
+  (`**/repomix-output*.xml`, the `repomix-*/` package directories). At most one
+  historical package may be retained as an archived snapshot; older duplicate
+  packages are removed from the tip and stay recoverable from git history.
+- **Large generated reports are not committed.** Report PDFs and similar bulk
+  binaries belong in release artifacts or off-repo storage, not the tree.
+- **Evidence transcripts are intentional.** Tracked `.log` transcripts under
+  `evidence/` are append-only audit records, explicitly exempted from the
+  `.gitignore` `*.log` rule (`!evidence/**/*.log`).
+- **Budget.** Keep the largest tracked file under ~2 MB (allowlisted binary
+  evidence may exceed this until relocated) and do not let the tracked worktree
+  grow without a documented reason.
+- **Current state.** The active-state pointer is
+  [`evidence/CURRENT_STATE.json`](../evidence/CURRENT_STATE.json) (schema:
+  [`docs/product/CURRENT_STATE_SCHEMA.md`](product/CURRENT_STATE_SCHEMA.md)).
+- **Historical root artifacts** live under [`docs/archive/`](archive/) with a
+  pointer; the authoritative gate ledger remains
+  `evidence/closeout/GATE_LEDGER.csv`.
